From 48ea5d6d2ee71559a3b34dbc1a2a05764cae0051 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:52:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A Rogue's two blades trail their own colours, and a dodge
 leaves the hero behind

The Rogue's looks the server can't make (Basin Battle's docs/rogue-roles.md, build plan 6).
PlayUnitAnimation's trail may be two colours, "AARRGGBB/AARRGGBB": the main hand's blade trails
the first and the off hand's the second, "-" leaving that hand without one, on 1.12's own weapon
swing trail (one a hand), which got one colour on both hands before. One colour is both, as ever.
PlayUnitAfterimage(unit, seconds[, alpha[, colour[, x, y, z[, standIn]]]]) leaves patch 0027's
frozen copy of a unit's own body and what it holds: where it is, or standing at a spot along the
ground (its rig's origin moved), keeping most of its alpha until near its end when it is longer
than half a second, and hiding a stand-in unit while it stands (the server's own body for the
look, which an older client shows instead); the copy goes with its stand-in if that goes first.
PlayUnitAfterimage(unit, 0) takes the unit's copies away. PlayUnitAfterimage joins the globals
past 1.12 and the VM surface golden. HasActionCombat() is 32: the server sends the two-colour
trail and its AI line only to this round.
